AB  - Selecting a modeling approach for HVAC systems should account for the characteristics of the available training data, particularly the extentto which they cover the intended operating domain. This study evaluated the replicative and predictive validity of grey-box, hybrid, andblack-box models for predicting the outlet-air temperature of an outdoor air-conditioning system(OAC) preheating coil in a semiconductorfacility. Training datasets with increasing operating-space coverage were constructed in a three-dimensional grid. Grey-box validity decreasedas coverage increased, whereas the hybrid model maintained relatively stable performance and achieved the highest predictive validity underlow coverage. The predictive MAE of the black-box model decreased markedly from 3.22 to 0.84°C as coverage increased. These findingsshow that the model selection should account for training data coverage and the intended prediction domain.
