AB  - This study distinguishes the underlying building energy prediction gap from the observable energy discrepancy by quantifying residualstochasticity. Four years (2018–2021) of electricity and gas data from 331 daycare centers and public health centers were compared withEnergyPlus simulations using annual weather data. The estimated stochastic variation averaged ±21.9% at the 99% confidence level. Thisimplies that the discrepancy from observed energy use may not necessarily represent a gap that should be eliminated, but may partly reflectstochastic realizations arising from building operation.
