UR  - https://www.dbpia.co.kr/journal/articleDetail?nodeId=NODE10563701
AB  - To  proper  control  of  electric  lighting  (e.g.  on/off,  multi-level,  dimming),  it  is  essential  to  predict  daylit  indoor  illuminance  at  the  workplane. For  the  use  of  the  Radiance-based  daylighting  simulation  tool,  solar  altitude,  solar  azimuth  and  Global  Horizontal  Irradiance  (GHI)  are required.  Rather  than  relying  on  the  measured  GHI  provided  in  off-line  from  a  nearby  weather  station,  this  study  presents  a  simplified method  to  directly  estimate  GHI  from  an  on-site  horizontal  illuminance.  For  this  purpose,  an  Artificial  Neural  Network  (ANN)  model  was developed  to  predict  GHI  with  data  of  solar  altitude,  solar  azimuth,  a  measured  illuminance,  and  cloud  cover.  It  is  found  that  the  ANN model  is  accurate  enough  (MBE:  2.4%,  CVRMSE:  15.7%).  This  proposed  model  will  be  integrated  to  daylit  prediction  model  and  on-line optimal  control  of  electric  lighting.
KW  - global horizontal irradiance
KW  - illuminance
KW  - artificial neural network
KW  - daylighting prediction
