AB  - This  paper  presents  a  Model-Predictive  Control  (MPC)  study  applied  to  a  heating  system  in  a  large  open  factory  building  in  Incheon,  South Korea.  Rather  than  resorting  to  a  full-blown  dynamic  simulation  model,  this  study  takes  a  lumped  minimalistic  approach  for  the  prediction indoor  air  temperatures  in  the  building.  It  was  found  that  the  lumped  simulation  model  is  accurate  enough  and  applicable  to  the  MPC  for the  building,  leading  to  energy  savings  by  52%.
