AB  - This paper suggests a methodology for predicting illuminance using Gaussian Process model. Based on one-point measured illuminance data, the authors developed Gaussian Process model which can predict an illuminance ratio between a reference point and points in interest. The Gaussian Process model uses solar altitude and azimuth as inputs. This approach was tested at a mechanical factory building for ten days. It is found that illuminance ratio changes with solar altitude and azimuth, and combination of Gaussian Process and one-point sensor data could describe indoor illuminances with a distribution of errors.
