UR  - https://www.auric.or.kr/user/rdoc/DocRdoc.aspx?dn=400986&returnVal=RD_R
AB  - Due to the lack of detailed building energy data (e.g. thermal properties of building envelopes, efficiencies of HVAC systems, hourlysub-metered energy data etc.), most of existing building energy benchmarking systems have used EUI (Energy Use Intensity, kWh/m2·yr) peruse type (office, school, etc). However, the EUI-based approach is closer to ‘energy use becnhmarking’ than ‘energy performancebenchmarking’. In this regard, this study aims to present a data-driven methodology to identify building’s thermal characteristics frommonthly energy use data, which will lead to objective performance comparison among buildings. In this study, ANN(Artifical NeuralNetwork) was utlized for the inverse identification and virtual traning data were generated from 10,000 samples of an EnergyPlus model byLHS. The ANN was validated with 14 existing buildings (CVRMSE 17.6%). This proposed approach will provide identification of theaforementioned unmeasured/uncertain thermal characteristics and will be used for objective performance comparison
KW  - building energy benchmakring
KW  - builidng performance
KW  - artificial neural network
KW  - identification
