UR  - https://www.dbpia.co.kr/journal/articleDetail?nodeId=NODE10518762
AB  - It  is  difficult  to  find  optimal  control  variables  for  lighting  system  in  an  existing  building  because  the  luminous  environment  is  influenced  by daylighting  that  continuously  vary  over  the  course  of  a  day.  In  addition,  the  luminous  environment  is  also  interplayed  with  (dimmable) electric  lighting.  Many  existing  optimization  algorithms  require  significant  effort  to  develop  an  accurate  simulation  model  as  well  as demanding  computation  time.  Recently,  reinforcement  learning  has  been  applied  to  complex  control  problems.  In  this  study,  DDPG  (Deep Deterministic  Policy  Gradient)  is  applied  to  dimmable  electric  lighting  system  in  an  existing  building.  It  is  shown  that  DDPG  can  be  used for  real-time  optimal  control  of  the  lighting  system  and  can  save  about  30%  of  lighting  energy  without  sacrifcing  luminous  uniformity  of  a given  space
